Description: Disable Doxygen autolinking for SAI metadata generation
 Doxygen 1.14 and later autolinks type names inside the SAI @xmlonly
 aliases, wrapping them in <ref> elements.  meta/parse.pl cannot parse those
 elements and reports invalid concatenated types.  Disabling autolinking
 restores the plain-text XML emitted by older Doxygen releases.
Origin: vendor, Canonical
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: Sheldon Qi <sheldon.qi@canonical.com>
Last-Update: 2026-07-22
---
 a/meta/Doxyfile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meta/Doxyfile b/meta/Doxyfile
index 4900fd9..c10de26 100644
--- a/meta/Doxyfile
+++ b/meta/Doxyfile
@@ -303,7 +303,7 @@ MARKDOWN_SUPPORT       = YES
 # or globally by setting AUTOLINK_SUPPORT to NO.
 # The default value is: YES.

-AUTOLINK_SUPPORT       = YES
+AUTOLINK_SUPPORT = NO

 # If you use STL classes (i.e. std::string, std::vector, etc.) but do not want
 # to include (a tag file for) the STL sources as input, then you should set this
